  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Which configuration actually runs",
      "items": [
        "QKV at T1 uses qkv8_r176, 24 output rows per CTA and six ring stages. T8 uses the narrow qkv8n_r144 build, 24 rows and five stages, with two accumulator sets.",
        "O at T1/T8 uses o8h_r88, 32 output rows and four stages. Sliced unpool uses slice8_r192, eight output rows and four stages. Both output BF16. Full-size O produces 8192 features."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "The packing is storage compression",
      "items": [
        "The input weights remain BF16 values. Packed values feed BF16 mma.sync. Out-of-range weights add delta-times-x corrections to the FP32 result. This differs from the MoE NVFP4 representation.",
        "Each selected short-token projection CTA covers the whole K reduction for its row tile. The selected QKV/O/unpool configs use one-CTA groups. No global split-K reduction is needed for these paths."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "What changes at T8 QKV",
      "items": [
        "The narrow override keeps the SK2 stream. Its escape workers read the needed x values directly from global memory, separate from the stage ring. The retained T8 profile names sk2_kernel_narrow; T1 names ordinary sk2_kernel.",
        "Projection PDL is disabled in this incumbent. Producer prefetch still occurs inside each kernel, but the diagram asserts no overlap with another launch. Unsupported preparation or failed numerical gates retain a library fallback."
      ]
    }
  ]
